WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:02.994
Reviewer: Last, what this first pass can't tell us.

2
00:00:02.994 --> 00:00:05.972
Reviewer: A screen reader shows whether things work as built,

3
00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:08.600
Reviewer: not whether they help the people they're for.

4
00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:12.747
Reviewer: These need people with disabilities, on their own devices and settings.

5
00:00:12.747 --> 00:00:15.375
Reviewer: I'll show each one on the page as we name it.

6
00:00:15.777 --> 00:00:17.458
Tester: First, Describe this page.

7
00:00:17.458 --> 00:00:22.501
Tester: I'll press Tab twice, to its button in the skip links, then Return to open it.

8
00:00:22.942 --> 00:00:24.594
Keyboard: Tab → link, Skip to content

9
00:00:24.594 --> 00:00:26.205
Keyboard: Tab → button, Describe this page

10
00:00:26.205 --> 00:00:28.016
Keyboard: Return → heading, The home page

11
00:00:28.016 --> 00:00:31.571
Tester: A dialog sits over the dimmed page, titled The home page:

12
00:00:31.571 --> 00:00:35.189
Tester: one sentence comparing it to the front page of a magazine,

13
00:00:35.189 --> 00:00:40.178
Tester: then a numbered list of its parts, top to bottom, and a Close button at the top.

14
00:00:40.178 --> 00:00:43.858
Tester: Does a description like this help someone picture the page?

15
00:00:43.858 --> 00:00:45.667
Tester: Is it too long, or too short?

16
00:00:45.667 --> 00:00:49.533
Tester: Blind people who use a screen reader every day should tell us,

17
00:00:49.533 --> 00:00:51.591
Tester: on VoiceOver and on JAWS or NVDA.

18
00:00:51.992 --> 00:00:54.242
Tester: I'll press Escape to close it.

19
00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:56.465
Keyboard: Escape → button, Describe this page

20
00:00:56.465 --> 00:01:01.200
Reviewer: Second, other screen readers and devices. We're back on the home page.

21
00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:03.905
Reviewer: This pass used VoiceOver in Safari only,

22
00:01:03.905 --> 00:01:09.316
Reviewer: and its biggest finding came from how Safari passes hidden content to VoiceOver.

23
00:01:09.316 --> 00:01:13.916
Reviewer: JAWS, NVDA, VoiceOver on iPhone and TalkBack all behave differently.

24
00:01:14.317 --> 00:01:15.574
Tester: Third, Set for you.

25
00:01:15.574 --> 00:01:20.671
Tester: I'll Tab across the header: my name, Writing, Work, Signal, Tools and Resume,

26
00:01:20.671 --> 00:01:23.717
Tester: then Set for you, and press Return to open it.

27
00:01:24.146 --> 00:01:25.755
Keyboard: Tab → link, Marcelo Paiva

28
00:01:25.755 --> 00:01:27.372
Keyboard: Tab → link, Writing

29
00:01:27.372 --> 00:01:28.999
Keyboard: Tab → link, Work

30
00:01:28.999 --> 00:01:30.606
Keyboard: Tab → link, Signal

31
00:01:30.606 --> 00:01:32.231
Keyboard: Tab → link, Tools

32
00:01:32.231 --> 00:01:33.862
Keyboard: Tab → link, Resume

33
00:01:33.862 --> 00:01:35.493
Keyboard: Tab → button, Set for you, collapsed

34
00:01:35.493 --> 00:01:37.301
Keyboard: Return → button, Set for you, expanded

35
00:01:37.301 --> 00:01:41.982
Tester: A small panel drops down with one sentence: show the drawings in calm color,

36
00:01:41.982 --> 00:01:45.369
Tester: with the theme following my device, and motion allowed.

37
00:01:45.369 --> 00:01:49.743
Tester: The home page as a list of essays. Each of those choices is a dropdown.

38
00:01:49.743 --> 00:01:52.391
Tester: Whether a sentence like that feels natural,

39
00:01:52.391 --> 00:01:56.641
Tester: and whether the announcements are enough, is for screen reader users,

40
00:01:56.641 --> 00:02:00.275
Tester: and people with cognitive or learning disabilities, to say.

41
00:02:00.676 --> 00:02:02.752
Tester: Escape closes the panel.

42
00:02:03.185 --> 00:02:04.985
Keyboard: Escape → button, Set for you, collapsed

43
00:02:04.985 --> 00:02:05.837
Reviewer: Fourth, motion.

44
00:02:05.837 --> 00:02:09.586
Reviewer: Under the introduction, a band of drawings drifts slowly sideways,

45
00:02:09.586 --> 00:02:13.959
Reviewer: and thin lines and points move across the dark background behind the heading.

46
00:02:13.959 --> 00:02:16.742
Reviewer: A pause button sits beside Set for you. It works…

47
00:02:16.742 --> 00:02:20.605
Reviewer: but is it found in time, and is the motion comfortable before it is?

48
00:02:20.605 --> 00:02:23.161
Reviewer: People with vestibular disorders can tell us.

49
00:02:23.561 --> 00:02:29.036
Tester: Fifth, zoom and magnification. I'll zoom in, pressing Command-Plus three times.

50
00:02:29.490 --> 00:02:31.700
Keyboard: Command-Plus: zooms the page

51
00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:33.900
Keyboard: Command-Plus: zooms the page

52
00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:35.880
Keyboard: Command-Plus: zooms the page

53
00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:40.404
Tester: The heading now fills most of the width, the header stays across the top,

54
00:02:40.404 --> 00:02:43.192
Tester: and the text sits over the moving background.

55
00:02:43.192 --> 00:02:47.655
Tester: People with low vision who use zoom or a screen magnifier should try it.

56
00:02:48.057 --> 00:02:51.582
Tester: Command-Zero puts the page back to its normal size.

57
00:02:52.015 --> 00:02:53.990
Keyboard: Command-0: back to actual size

58
00:02:53.990 --> 00:02:56.420
Reviewer: Sixth, voice control and switch access.

59
00:02:56.420 --> 00:03:01.405
Reviewer: Names were checked for what a screen reader says, not for what people say aloud,

60
00:03:01.405 --> 00:03:06.515
Reviewer: and the home page has more than fifty stops for someone moving one step at a time.

61
00:03:06.916 --> 00:03:08.425
Tester: And last, the collage.

62
00:03:08.425 --> 00:03:13.090
Tester: I'll press Return to open Set for you again, then Tab past Drawings,

63
00:03:13.090 --> 00:03:15.766
Tester: Theme and Motion, to its last dropdown.

64
00:03:16.191 --> 00:03:18.224
Keyboard: Return → button, Set for you, expanded

65
00:03:18.224 --> 00:03:19.823
Keyboard: Tab → pop-up button, Drawings, in calm color

66
00:03:19.823 --> 00:03:21.448
Keyboard: Tab → pop-up button, Theme, following my device

67
00:03:21.448 --> 00:03:23.037
Keyboard: Tab → pop-up button, Motion, allowed

68
00:03:23.037 --> 00:03:24.644
Keyboard: Tab → pop-up button, Home page, a list of essays

69
00:03:24.644 --> 00:03:26.144
Keyboard: Focus is on → pop-up button, Home page, a list of essays

70
00:03:25.603 --> 00:03:28.655
Tester: The Home page dropdown reads a list of essays.

71
00:03:28.655 --> 00:03:34.096
Tester: Choosing a collage of drawings there turns the home page into a field of pictures.

72
00:03:34.096 --> 00:03:36.153
Tester: This pass tested the list only.

73
00:03:36.554 --> 00:03:38.404
Tester: Escape closes it.

74
00:03:38.838 --> 00:03:40.620
Keyboard: Escape → button, Set for you, collapsed

75
00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:42.859
Tester: That's the end of the first pass.

76
00:03:42.859 --> 00:03:47.745
Tester: Six problems found on the page: five fixed and live, and one still open.

77
00:03:48.148 --> 00:03:50.273
Reviewer: The next test is with people.
